 <shortdesc>Move Bounds</shortdesc>
 <longdesc><para unique="1261284">
   <string>BNDMOV moves a pair of lower and upper bound values from the source operand (the second operand) to the destination (the first operand). Each operation is 128-bit move. The exceptions are same as the MOV instruction. The memory format for loading/store bounds in 64-bit mode is shown in </string><link linkend="34586: 05_FigureFrame: Figure 10-8. Layout of the Bounds Registers BND0-BND3"><string>Figure&#160;3&#8209;5</string></link><string>.</string></para>
