   <string>None.</string></para>
  </subsection>
 <subsection title="Protected Mode Exceptions">
  <variablelist>
   <variablelistentry>
    <term><string>#UD</string></term>
    <listitem><string>If the LOCK prefix is used but the destination is not a memory operand.</string></listitem>
    <listitem><string>If ModRM.r/m encodes BND4-BND7 when Intel MPX is enabled.</string></listitem>
    <listitem><string>If 67H prefix is not used and CS.D=0.</string></listitem>
    <listitem><string>If 67H prefix is used and CS.D=1.</string></listitem>
    </variablelistentry>
   <variablelistentry>
    <term><string>#SS(0)</string></term>
    <listitem><string>If the memory operand effective address is outside the SS segment limit.</string></listitem>
    </variablelistentry>
   <variablelistentry>
    <term><string>#GP(0)</string></term>
    <listitem><string>If the memory operand effective address is outside the CS, DS, ES, FS, or GS segment limit.</string></listitem>
    <listitem><string>If the destination operand points to a non-writable segment</string></listitem>
    <listitem><string>If the DS, ES, FS, or GS segment register contains a NULL segment selector.</string></listitem>
    </variablelistentry>
   <variablelistentry>
    <term><string>#AC(0)</string></term>
    <listitem><string>If alignment checking is enabled and an unaligned memory reference is made while CPL is 3.</string></listitem>
    </variablelistentry>
   <variablelistentry>
    <term><string>#PF(fault code)</string></term>
    <listitem><string>If a page fault occurs.</string></listitem>
    </variablelistentry>
   </variablelist>
  </subsection>
